cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certified Max-Cut incumbents or witnesses, please cite this repository."
title: "Stanford G-set Max-Cut: Proof-Carrying Incumbent Release"
authors:
  - family-names: Grebeshok
    given-names: Aleksandr
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Certified feasible Max-Cut solutions (proof-carrying incumbents) for five canonical
  unweighted Stanford G-set instances (G1, G2, G3, G14, G22). Each instance ships with
  its graph, a binary witness partition vector, SHA-256 checksums, and an autonomous
  pure-Python verifier that recomputes the cut value from the graph alone. For G22 the
  witness of value 13359 matches the established modern best known solution of the
  literature (e.g. Benlic & Hao, 2013). The release certifies feasible lower bounds,
  not global optimality.
keywords:
  - max-cut
  - combinatorial optimization
  - benchmark
  - Stanford G-set
  - proof-carrying data
  - certified solutions
type: dataset
